{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לא תראה את שור אחיך", :translit "lo tir'eh et shor achicha", :gloss "you shall not see your brother's ox"} {:he "והתעלמת", :translit "vehit'alamt", :gloss "and you shall hide yourself"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "smikhut parshiyot: semikhut of hashavat avedah to the prohibition on a kohen becoming tameh, yielding the exemption of והתעלמת for a kohen in a cemetery"} {:kind :other, :note "smikhut parshiyot: semikhut of והתעלמת to the preceding clause teaches that one who returns his own lost items must also return those of his fellow"}], :frame {:text "The law of hashavat avedah applies even when significant personal inconvenience or transgression is involved. A kohen who encounters a lost item in a cemetery is nonetheless obligated, for Leviticus 21:1 prohibits a kohen from becoming tameh for the dead, yet the juxtaposition of our verse to that passage (Deut. 21:23–22:1) establishes that the obligation stands. The verb והתעלמת itself is expounded: Sifrei Devarim 252 reads it as 'you may hide yourself' only when the loss is your own, but for your fellow's loss you must act. The further juxtaposition within our verse teaches that one who is vigilant about his own property must show equal vigilance for his fellow's.", :sources ["Leviticus 21:1" "Deuteronomy 21:23" "Deuteronomy 22:1-3" "Sifrei Devarim 252"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "smikhut parshiyot: semikhut of hashavat avedah to the prohibition on a kohen becoming tameh, yielding the exemption of והתעלמת for a kohen in a cemetery", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "smikhut parshiyot: semikhut of והתעלמת to the preceding clause teaches that one who returns his own lost items must also return those of his fellow", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:06.197457360Z", :model "glm-5.2"}